\viewkind4\uc1\pard\nowidctlpar\tx720\tx2280\cf1\kerning2\f0\fs24 Kent Edwards and Chris Chitester from the Office of Sustainability presented a follow-up from the November 19, 2024, Commission Meeting regarding Energy Savings Performance Contracting (ESPC). Mr. Chitester stated that ESPC was a financing mechanism that allowed public agencies to implement energy efficiency improvements, resulting in significant cost savings and sustainability benefits without requiring any upfront taxpayer capital investment. He mentioned that the energy cost savings improvements generated would fund the project, resulting in a cost-saving neutral solution. \par
\par
Mr. Edwards stated that ESPC offers several advantages, such as energy cost savings, budget preservation, reduced maintenance expenses, and environmental sustainability. He noted navigating through the ESPC process requires collaboration from staff in finance, legal, and facilities management. Mr. Edwards recommended the City continue researching ESPC to understand its implementation for Delray Beach and return to the Commission with a detailed presentation.\par
\cf0\par
The Commission thanked Mr. Edwards and Mr. Chitester for their efforts.\cf1\kerning0\f1\par
}

