\viewkind4\uc1\pard\nowidctlpar\tx720\cf1\f0\fs24 Laura Simon, Executive Director of the Downtown Development Authority (DDA), and Suzanne Boyd, Marketing Director, presented their recommendations for new logos to rebrand the Old School Square Complex. \par
\par
During the presentation, Ms. Simon emphasized the importance of a public voting campaign, allowing the community to play a vital role in selecting a design that reflects the shared history of the communities' vibrant culture and vision for the future. She stated their goal was to create a branded house that honors the past while establishing a foundation for the next 100 years. Once the submissions are collected, the public would have the opportunity to vote on the final logo, promoting community engagement. The artist whose design received the most votes would be selected as the winner. Ms. Simon also mentioned the proposed timeline was expected to be 18-20 weeks from the reveal.\par
\par
The Commission expressed their excitement and support for the new concepts introduced by the DDA.\f1\par
}

