\viewkind4\uc1\pard\kerning2\f0\fs24 Terrence Moore, City Manager, stated that Missie Barletto, Public Works Director, was present to provide an overview of the roadway reconstruction program in response to a public comment made by a resident during a previous meeting.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\kerning0\f1 Ms. Barletto provided a presentation explaining that the City evaluates its streets using a Pavement Condition Index (PCI). This system allows for real-time assessments and updates of the PCI, which helps determine the appropriate treatment and maintenance for the roadways. She emphasized that this approach enables the City to prioritize the needs of each roadway effectively. She explained that the previous funding for road maintenance came from an infrastructure surtax, which has now expired. However, she mentioned that the City is considering implementing a new transportation surtax to replace the expired infrastructure tax. Ms. Barletto provided details on current road conditions, planned improvement levels for each location, and associated costs based on PCI ratings. She mentioned that many current roadway improvements were being funded through grants.\par
\par
The Commission discussed the presentation and acknowledged the importance of securing funding to preserve and maintain the City's roads before they deteriorate to the point where repair costs increase significantly. The Commission thanked Ms. Barletto for her comprehensive presentation.\cf1\f2\par
}

