{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Police Chief Darrell Hunter and Lt. Matthew Naparstek presented an update on the School Zone Speed Camera Program, reporting that cameras have been installed at eight of the nine schools, with Carver Middle School pending due to ongoing construction. They explained that the program is currently in an education and warning phase only, and no citations are being issued at this time. Enforcement, they noted, will follow state law timelines tied to school start and end times.\par
\par
Commissioners raised concerns about the lack of flashing beacons at some schools, confusing signage and enforcement times, and the need for expanded public education. In response, Chief Hunter stated that staff will work with the schools, RedSpeed, Public Works, and the Communications Department to improve signage, outreach, and overall consistency before the program officially goes live.\par
}

