{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Assistant Chief Procurement Officer Casetra Thompson presented proposed amendments to the City\rquote s Purchasing Policies and Procedures Manual, noting that it has not been updated since 2017. She explained that the revisions are intended to reflect increased costs of goods and services, improve administrative efficiency, and ensure consistent application of procurement rules. Key changes included raising the City Manager\rquote s approval authority for non-contract vendor spending from $65,000 to $100,000 annually, adding exemptions for contractually obligated purchases related to special events such as the Delray Beach Open and for calibration or servicing of police and fire equipment, and streamlining procurement processes for small-dollar and urgent purchases to reduce delays and administrative burden.\par
\par
Ms. Gelin added that the revisions clarify ambiguities in the current manual and enhance efficiency while still maintaining checks and balances through review by Procurement, the City Attorney\rquote s Office, and the City Manager\rquote s Office. \par
\par
Commissioners expressed support for the updates, citing inflationary pressures and the need for greater operational flexibility.\par
}

