\viewkind4\uc1\pard\kerning2\f0\fs24 Mike Caruso, Palm Beach County Clerk of the Circuit Court and Comptroller, presented on scams and property fraud affecting residents, outlining priorities set after his August 2025 election such as modernizing the county\rquote s $10 billion vendor payment system, advocating for a statewide searchable records database, maintaining conservative investment practices, and protecting residents-especially seniors from guardianship and property deed fraud. He highlighted the growing scale and sophistication of scams, including fake calls about unpaid citations or jury duty and property deed fraud schemes using fraudulent quitclaim deeds, loans, and resales before owners are aware, and described the Clerk\rquote s free Property Fraud Alert (PFA) system that emails notifications of recorded documents, allows up to five contacts, and supports rapid response in coordination with law enforcement, while offering his assistance and direct contact to help residents avoid becoming victims.\f1 \par
