\par
\pard Missie Barletto, Public Works Director, reported that three Transportation Planning Agency (TPA) projects: North Swinton Avenue, Barwick Road, and Lindell Boulevard are all progressing largely on schedule, with North Swinton Avenue slightly behind in phase one but nearing completion. Phase two is expected to move faster. Barwick Road was about halfway complete and projected to finish around mid-summer (July), and Lindell Boulevard was ahead of schedule and expected to be substantially completed in May. Ms. Barletto addressed questions about pedestrian level decorative lighting, explaining those lights are required for federally funded bicycle and pedestrian improvement projects. She noted the lights are installed through the Florida Power & Light contract, meaning the City does not own or maintain the poles and they do not add direct maintenance costs to the City.\par
\pard\sl276\slmult1\par
Commissioner Casale appreciated Mr. Harden raising questions, but expressed concern about staff spending time preparing full presentations when only one resident raises an issue. She suggested that extensive presentations might be more appropriate when concerns come from a larger group of residents. Mayor Carney responded that it has long been the City\rquote s practice for the City Manager to publicly respond to concerns and Mr. Moore agreed, stating that when issues are raised publicly before the Commission it is appropriate to provide public clarification for the record, and that preparing such updates is not overly time-consuming.\par
\par
Mayor Carney thanked staff for the informative update.\cf1\kerning0\f1\par
}

