\par
Commissioner Casale inquired about department revenue, noting that roof permits were at zero compared to the prior year. She also asked about pool permits and other permits, including whether the revenue was moving to building. Anthea Gianniotes, Development Services Director, explained that Florida Building Code related permits were required to go into the building fund rather than the general fund. She stated roof permits had remained in the general fund and were not supposed to be there, so the general fund account showed zero revenue after the adjustment. \par
\par
Additionally, Commissioner Casale asked Mr. Moore that future budgets provide more detail on special event costs, including police overtime and regular costs for events.\par
}

