{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\kerning2\f0\fs24 Mr. Moore summarized a memorandum from CBIZ CPAs addressing concerns raised by resident Jason Bodnick during the September 22, 2026, budget public hearing regarding $55 million in annual expenditures allegedly unaccounted for based on his review of the City\rquote s annual comprehensive financial reports from 2015 through 2024. The memorandum explained that general fund expenditures are reported using the modified accrual basis of accounting and include capital asset acquisitions, debt-related payments, and Community Redevelopment Agency (CRA) activities. CRA tax increment payments increased from $7.7 million in FY 2015 to more than $21 million in FY 2024. Mr. Moore stated that expenditure trends should be evaluated in the context of approved budgets, accounting methods, capital investments, debt-related expenditures, CRA expenditures, personnel costs, and relevant operational, economic, and policy considerations. He stated that the review alleviated concerns about millions of dollars not being accounted for and distributed copies of the memorandum to the Commission.\par
\par
Commissioner Casale requested that such information be provided to the Commission when received, noting that the initial information raised questions. Mr. Moore explained that the memorandum was dated October 2 but received on October 5, and stated that he presented the findings orally because the information was received the previous day. He reiterated that he would continue to provide information to the Commission in advance.\par
\par
Mr. Moore clarified that the former agricultural reserve property under consideration for an Islamic center school is located in unincorporated Palm Beach County, west of Delray Beach\rquote s corporate limits. He stated that the City of Delray Beach has no jurisdiction or role in the approval process, which falls under the authority of the Palm Beach County Board of County Commissioners.\par
\par
Mr. Moore reported that the Lindell Boulevard and Barwick Road infrastructure improvements are substantially completed and will be closed out soon.\cf1\kerning0\f1\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}}
