\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Missie Barletto, Public Works Director, presented the estimated financial impact of implementing free parking Wednesdays year-round. She reported that during the summer pilot, average parking occupancy decreased by approximately 2%, while daily turnover increased by 22.7% and the average length of stay decreased by approximately 47 minutes. She identified the participating garages and surface lots and estimated the annual revenue impact at approximately $220,000, or an average of $4,216 per Wednesday. She stated that a resolution would be brought back on November 17 for consideration on the consent agenda. She clarified that the figures were revenue projections and that actual revenue information was still being researched.\par
\par
Vice Mayor Burns asked whether the figures were estimates. Commissioner Casale, Commissioner Mollica, and Deputy Vice Mayor Markert expressed support for continuing free parking Wednesdays, citing positive feedback from downtown merchants and residents. \par
\par
Mayor Carney stated that there was consensus to make free parking Wednesdays a permanent feature. The Commission agreed to bring back a resolution on November 17, 2026, with an effective date of December 1, 2026.\par
}

